From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BerryMC <BerryMC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:47:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Update netty to 4.1.141.Final

Bump netty-all from 4.1.77.Final (early 2022) to the latest 4.1.x
release, pulling in two years of CVE fixes and JDK 21+ compatibility
improvements (reduced sun.misc.Unsafe reliance on modern JVMs).

All netty usage in this codebase is on stable 4.1 APIs (ServerBootstrap,
ChannelInitializer, Nio/Epoll event loops, codecs, FlushConsolidation
Handler, ReadTimeoutHandler, FastThreadLocalThread, AttributeKey), so
this is a drop-in bump. ProtocolLib/ProtocolSupport on 1.12.2 use the
same stable surface; report any plugin-side netty issues upstream.

diff --git a/pom.xml b/pom.xml
index 9c7f0d20b078459eaf0650adab102ca06bc904bd..6e559977dfbabcbbe8ecf82b0dd9af654ee7c2ed 100644
--- a/pom.xml
+++ b/pom.xml
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
         <dependency>
             <groupId>io.netty</groupId>
             <artifactId>netty-all</artifactId>
-            <version>4.1.77.Final</version>
+            <version>4.1.141.Final</version>
             <scope>compile</scope>
         </dependency>
         <dependency>
